WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.852
Videos live in your organisation’s video library.

00:00:03.802 --> 00:00:07.226
Upload once and use them in any course.

00:00:07.226 --> 00:00:12.513
They are prepared for streaming, so learners on slow connections can watch too.

00:00:13.484 --> 00:00:18.642
Uploads keep going while you work, and carry on after a dropped connection.

00:00:18.592 --> 00:00:22.785
When it is ready, open the video to add captions.

00:00:27.429 --> 00:00:34.384
Upload a caption file, or let speech recognition make them for you and correct them in the caption editor.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:39.177
Captions help everyone, and power the transcript learners can read.

00:00:40.141 --> 00:00:44.557
In a lesson, add a Video block and choose it from the library.

00:00:44.507 --> 00:00:49.923
YouTube and Vimeo links work too: paste the link and the title is filled in.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:54.466
Add chapters so learners can jump to each part.

00:00:54.416 --> 00:01:02.073
And add a question during the video: at the time you choose, the video pauses and asks one of this step’s questions.
